{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow","id":809870,"title":"[Homebrew] Devotion: Crushing Blow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-15T15:16:14-08:00","id":809870,"title":"[Homebrew] Devotion: Crushing Blow","content":"One of my fellow players is a big fan of Vigor and Brawl, and wants to deal some Lethal damage, but not so much interested in Weaponry or Protean. It doesn't fit the character's background to want to learn to use a bladed weapon or find a Gangrel to teach them how to sprout claws, so I'm trying to develop a simple Devotion as an alternate or extra ability to add to Vigor. To that end, here's a short draft; I've given the Devotion a start point of 3 points in Vigor as a baseline. I'd welcome any input or suggestions.<br /> <br /> <b><i>CRUSHING BLOW</i><br /> (Vigor </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <br /> Normally, Vigor on its own suits most Kindred just fine. Some, however, take a special pleasure in the idea of crushing foes or rending objects with their bare limbs with even greater, more terrifying ease, and they don't care for the courtly refinements of Kindred Dueling or the out-and-out ferocity of Protean's <i>Unnatural Aspect.</i> This Devotion simply infuses a Kindred with a greater degree of might above what Vigor normally affords them. Attempting to wield all but the sturdiest of objects instead of bare hands doesn't work; blades shatter and baseball bats snap on impact\u2014if they're not simply crushed in the grip of their wielder. Those who use <i>Crushing Blow</i> don't usually worry about such niceties as melee weapons, though; their fists speak loudly enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <br /> By concentrating and spending a point of Vitae, a Kindred may infuse their dead limbs with a horrific degree of force\u2014sometimes manifesting as an icy alabaster sheen to their skin like polished marble, or vivid crimson or cold blue traceries of their blood vessels standing to the surface as power thrums through them.<br /> <br /> For the duration of the scene, the Kindred may deal Lethal damage with Brawl attacks, even against Kindred or other targets that would normally downgrade Lethal to Bashing; for breaking or destroying inanimate objects, the user's dots in Vigor are added as a bonus to the roll. Ribs and jaws shatter under the attacker's fists like fine china, and steel fire doors cave in like wet cardboard.<br /> <br /> <i>Crushing Blow</i> may also be further enhanced if the Kindred has the Vitae to spend on Vigor's normal effects, although within limits; spending Vitae to add Vigor as a bonus to Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry still gains those extra dice, but lifting and hurling especially large objects (such as a car) still only deals Lethal damage to Kindred. Aggravated damage is still outside the remit of this Devotion . . . although there are some whispers of especially Vigor-talented or elder Kindred who can manifest it in an even more puissant form<i>. </i><br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.<br /> <br /> (Dealing Aggravated damage requires Vigor \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and Resilience \u2022<span style=\"font-size:10px\">, <span style=\"font-size:12px\">adds <i>double </i>the Kindred's dots in Vigor to breaking objects,</span></span> and costs 3 Experience.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 01-15-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T15:26:37-08:00","id":809877,"title":"","content":"When you use the active effect of Vigor in combat, its treated as a Lethal weapon with a modifier equal to your <i>dots in Vigor</i>, so I don't see the necessity for this Devotion out of hand. Somebody with Vigor 3 needs to spend 1 Vitae to punch people with the capacity for hurting equal to a fireaxe, and that's not even counting the minimal 1 success required to hit, which also deals Lethal. Your player needs to spend 1 Vitae to deal 4L to a mortal on a turn, what's not to like?<br /> <br /> I'd maybe make a Vigor 2, Celerity 1 Devotion that might offer the Armor Piercing effect on the punch, but this just seems redundant with base Vigor.<br /> <br /> Looking more closely, you have it doing lethal damage even to Kindred. How? Gangrel need Protean 4 claws in order to do that, and it's because Unnatural Aspect is magic, not because of massive bodily destruction.<br /> <br /> A vampire with Vigor is just a stronger vampire, there's nothing here to suggest it should give him the capability to do lethal damage to other Kindred through this devotion.<br /> <br /> Tell him to use his fangs. Vigor can apply to those after all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T15:47:25-08:00","id":809883,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure I have the most updated version of VtR 2.0 (with the hybrid VtR 1.0 / Blood &amp; Smoke cover), and it doesn't seem to say anything about Vigor causing Lethal damage, just adding to Strength (and the active version just adds more dots rather than converting to Lethal; the only mention of Lethal damage I see is hurling large objects like motorcycles or cars). If there's been another change to the errata and a revision to the PDF, I'll look for it, but that still leaves only Lethal damage being done to mortals (unless you have enough Vigor to lift a Size 10 object, which is the only exception there).<br /> <br /> For the question of how it does Lethal damage to Kindred, the same question could apply to Protean 2 vs Protean 4. One does Lethal with claws (Feral Aspect); one does Lethal with claws even to Kindred (Unnatural Aspect). The only difference? The latter is . . . more Protean-y . . . is the only real answer. Thus, concentrating on Vigor to bring about some sort of supernatural boost that harms even Kindred to a greater degree seems to make sense in about the same way.<br /> <br /> I began with just the assumption of someone with Strength 2, Brawl 2; Protean 4 gives them a total dice pool of 6, all lethal, and with 2 armor piercing to boot.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, someone with Vigor 3 has a base pool of 7 dice\u2014all bashing (unless the Lethal damage thing has indeed changed, which still is obviated vs Kindred); that breaks down to 3 lethal, 1 bashing, if you go by converting the cost of Vitae expended to heal the injury. (Even spending Vitae for 1 round in that case makes it the equivalent of 5 Lethal.) In either case with Vigor, there's no armor piercing effect as there is with Protean; the only difference is that you have more dice added to your pool (especially if you spend Vitae to double your effective Vigor dots), thus reducing the chance of a target's defense mitigating the attack.<br /> <br /> Simply put, I wanted to come up with a way of dealing just plain Lethal damage for those who don't have the wherewithal or desire to learn how to do so with anything other than their own unarmed strikes. True, you can effectively deal Lethal damage as has been broken down in the previous paragraph, but this is more about focusing the Discipline to get a directly Lethal effect regardless of the target.<br /> <br /> The person in question is aware of the fangs idea, but it also doesn't fit their character to start biting their opponents; they genuinely just like the idea of getting to, as H.O.L. puts it, <i>Make Someone Stop Living With Your Fists</i>, hence this attempt at a Devotion. (Your idea about combining Vigor and Celerity for Armor Piercing is indeed a neat idea, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 01-15-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:16:15-08:00","id":809900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809883#post809883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure I have the most updated version of VtR 2.0 (with the hybrid VtR 1.0 / Blood &amp; Smoke cover), and it doesn't seem to say anything about Vigor causing Lethal damage, just adding to Strength (and the active version just adds more dots rather than converting to Lethal; the only mention of Lethal damage I see is hurling large objects like motorcycles or cars). If there's been another change to the errata and a revision to the PDF, I'll look for it, but that still leaves only Lethal damage being done to mortals (unless you have enough Vigor to lift a Size 10 object, which is the only exception there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, you add your dots in Vigor as a <b>&quot;weapon bonus&quot;</b> upon using Vigor's first active effect. If you look at page 179, that explains 'every weapon deals lethal to mortals.' That's why Vigor causes lethal damage to mortals when using its active effect. Admittedly, it takes a bit of page jumping and isn't explicit, so it's easy to overlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:17:42-08:00","id":809903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809883#post809883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure I have the most updated version of VtR 2.0 (with the hybrid VtR 1.0 / Blood &amp; Smoke cover), and it doesn't seem to say anything about Vigor causing Lethal damage, just adding to Strength (and the active version just adds more dots rather than converting to Lethal; the only mention of Lethal damage I see is hurling large objects like motorcycles or cars). If there's been another change to the errata and a revision to the PDF, I'll look for it, but that still leaves only Lethal damage being done to mortals (unless you have enough Vigor to lift a Size 10 object, which is the only exception there).</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're looking for is this active effect &quot;Add her dots in Vigor as a weapon bonus to all Athletics, Brawl, and Weaponry attacks made this turn.&quot; That weapon bonus gives your fists a Damage Modifier equal to your vigor dots, and anything with a Damage Modifier does lethal damage to mortals. This isn't the result of sorcery or a supernatural effect, it just means you're spending Vitae to invigorate your strength and hurt someone <i>more </i>with a punch than you might otherwise.<br /> <br /> For the question of how it does Lethal damage to Kindred, the same question could apply to Protean 2 vs Protean 4. One does Lethal with claws (Feral Aspect); one does Lethal with claws even to Kindred (Unnatural Aspect). The only difference? The latter is . . . more Protean-y . . . is the only real answer. Thus, concentrating on Vigor to bring about some sort of supernatural boost that harms even Kindred to a greater degree seems to make sense in about the same way.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> No, the idea behind the different claws doing damage is that the unnatural aspect renders them as more than mundane claws, such that they do lethal damage even to Kindred. It's the same reason that Kindred base fangs do lethal damage as part of the template. Because they're mystical on a level that lesser forms of damage aren't. Vigor doesn't naturally lend itself to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809883#post809883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I began with just the assumption of someone with Strength 2, Brawl 2; Protean 4 gives them a total dice pool of 6, all lethal, and with 2 armor piercing to boot.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, someone with Vigor 3 has a base pool of 7 dice\u2014all bashing (unless the Lethal damage thing has indeed changed, which still is obviated vs Kindred); that breaks down to 3 lethal, 1 bashing, if you go by converting the cost of Vitae expended to heal the injury. (Even spending Vitae for 1 round in that case makes it the equivalent of 5 Lethal.) In either case with Vigor, there's no armor piercing effect as there is with Protean; the only difference is that you have more dice added to your pool (especially if you spend Vitae to double your effective Vigor dots), thus reducing the chance of a target's defense mitigating the attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind that the person with Vigor 4 will have a larger dicepool, he'll also be hitting for 5L minimum every time he spends a Vitae, which is perfectly nasty in its own right. Protean 4 and Vigor 4 are not exactly equivalent anyway, as they fulfill different functions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809883#post809883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I wanted to come up with a way of dealing just plain Lethal damage for those who don't have the wherewithal or desire to learn how to do so with anything other than their own unarmed strikes. True, you can effectively deal Lethal damage as has been broken down in the previous paragraph, but this is more about focusing the Discipline to get a directly Lethal effect regardless of the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell him to spend Vitae to hit harder with Vigor. The rollover is what will kill Kindred. Unless there's something about this devotion that makes the character's fists carry some kind of supernatural effect a la Protean 4 or a Vampire's Fangs (these are sort of playing with predatory symbolism, it should also be observed) then there's no reason for it to inherently do lethal to Kindred. I'm not suggesting that such a Devotion can't exist, just that it needs that mystical component as an explicit rational for it to differ from mundane Vigor. Furthermore, I might suggest as a drawback that if you're paying 1 Vitae for a Scene for what is arguably less effective than straight up <i>using Vigor </i>than maybe while using this effect, you can't access the other active effects of Vigor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809883#post809883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The person in question is aware of the fangs idea, but it also doesn't fit their character to start biting their opponents; they genuinely just like the idea of getting to, as H.O.L. puts it, <i>Make Someone Stop Living With Your Fists</i>, hence this attempt at a Devotion. (Your idea about combining Vigor and Celerity for Armor Piercing is indeed a neat idea, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Like I said, for it to not be redundant and pass conceptual muster in Requiem, it needs more of a reason for why it does lethal damage even to Vampires. That's the key issue here, though your misunderstanding of how Vigor works might also contribute to his believed need for this Devotion.<br /> <br /> Really, the key here is to understand how Vigor works. If you have Vigor 3 and spend 1 Vitae, when you hit them you will at least do 4L to a mortal, and 4B to a vampire. If you hit said vampire twice, you're rolling over into Lethal damage already, and a third hit will torpor him if he has average Stamina. That's really powerful. It's really good. It's part of what makes Vigor great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:01:33-08:00","id":809930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809900#post809900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, you add your dots in Vigor as a <b>&amp;quot;weapon bonus&amp;quot;</b> upon using Vigor's first active effect. If you look at page 179, that explains 'every weapon deals lethal to mortals.' That's why Vigor causes lethal damage to mortals when using its active effect. Admittedly, it takes a bit of page jumping and isn't explicit, so it's easy to overlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah hah, now that's <i>definitely </i>helpful to know. I kept feeling like I was missing something. All the skipping around does indeed add some confusion, so my thanks to both of you.<br /> <br /> As for Leetsepeak's mention of feral symbolism, there are some predatory creatures that don't necessarily rely on claws and fangs. An enraged gorilla or other ape, for example, is just as likely to charge you and slam you into something or pummel you with fists as they are to bite, and even scorpions, while they do have claws, use them to grab and crush, not rip and tear. Anyway, symbolism in that fashion isn't really the key here (although I think I see it's important for how you perceive matters in your game), because I'm looking more for a way for the character to use what they have instead of just telling them, &quot;Learn Protean,&quot; or, &quot;Just bite them.&quot; (Which IIRC requires either Frenzy or Riding the Wave or grappling first to deal biting damage, and again, isn't what they're seeking.)<br /> <br /> I'd still regard someone who's focused on Vigor (itself a terrifying power, yes) to have something above and beyond its basis, even a little. The text itself describes Vigor as making someone supernaturally strong, and the Vitae boost making their strikes Lethal to mortals, so I'd see Crushing Blow as a further extension of that concept alone: You're making supernatural strength work in a more focused, mystical manner that should make Kindred blink.<br /> <br /> What I'm looking to do is give them a chance to be on par with the Protean and Kindred Dueling crowd . . . to, as Vigor's description even says, &quot;kick like a freight train&quot; and &quot;rend steel with their bare hands.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, you can punch someone into torpor with a few Vigor strikes if you're lucky, but with Protean, or a sharp blade and Kindred Dueling, you can do it even faster (in two hits, or even one hit if you're really good or lucky).<br /> <br /> I'm aware that some may see the Devotion as possibly redundant, but my point is to let the player have a chance to feel they're doing something unique instead of just &quot;Spending a Vitae for extra dice.&quot; (This is also why the added damage to objects is added in as a fun side concept). I've recently been reading an article on improving tabletop games, and one suggestion is basically, whether player or ST, &quot;Find a way to say yes.&quot; (Within reason; letting someone assassinate the Prince on their first night out may be a bit too far, for example). Simply put, I'm trying to say yes, and a chance for them to research and develop a Devotion might fit the bill.<br /> <br /> (N.B. Ultimately, I'm looking to see if this idea is mechanically balanced with regard to prerequisites and comparable abilities. So far, I've only read that it seems redundant, which, if the player wants to spend XP and time on something that's just another approach to the same end, would be their choice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 01-15-2016, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:30:37-08:00","id":809948,"title":"","content":"And...what about dealing tilts like arm wrack with this devotion (even to kindred)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:32:54-08:00","id":809949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809948#post809948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And...what about dealing tilts like arm wrack with this devotion (even to kindred)?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the penalties and effects would still apply, since Tilts such as Arm Wrack aren't dependant on the type of damage, just how much net damage you do compared to the target's Stamina.<br /> <br /> If the question is inverted and one asks what happens to the user of the Devotion if they experience such a Tilt, the answer would be the same, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:16:58-08:00","id":810145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/809870-homebrew-devotion-crushing-blow?p=809949#post809949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, the penalties and effects would still apply, since Tilts such as Arm Wrack aren't dependant on the type of damage, just how much net damage you do compared to the target's Stamina.<br /> <br /> If the question is inverted and one asks what happens to the user of the Devotion if they experience such a Tilt, the answer would be the same, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant something similar to butchery (a gift of werewolf) that says: &quot;whenever the<br /> Rahu hits a foe with an unarmed attack (including teeth and<br /> claws), or is hit by a foe, he may apply one of the following<br /> Tilts to it regardless of whether the attack deals any damage:<br /> Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, Knocked Down, Leg Wrack.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems nice to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T02:34:54-08:00","id":810151,"title":"","content":"Well, Crushing Blow's lupine namesake causes a defense penalty, plus lethal if the werewolf is in human form at the time (because that's the only time they can't do it naturally). So maybe the same here would work, plus it doing lethal to vampires because it's channelling the Beast through one's fists or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:58:50-08:00","id":810251,"title":"","content":"When I say it's redundant for the record, I don't mean it's redundant with Protean or Fangs, but with Vigor itself, because Vigor does what he wants this to do better than the proposed effect.<br /> <br /> The mystical component of unnatural aspect is what makes its claws distinct from those at Protean 2, and if you want a broad mechanical suggestion for what should allow this to do lethal damage to Kindred it's that it needs to do 1 of two things: it needs to either cause massive bodily harm or it needs to be magical. If you want a suggestion that skews towards the more powerful, I'd make it a Vigor 4 devotion that modified the active effect so that it's even more explosively damaging but lowers the base damage. So Vigor 4 is basically a 4L weapon, right? So with this Devotion, it could instead be Vigor - 2 Weapon Modifier, but it deals aggravated to mundane foes, reflecting the massive bodily harm that it does. Against Kindred t would downgrade, but to lethal rather than bashing. The kind of strength this reflects is the kind that lets the Kindred quite literally rip a mortal's arm off, and to Kindred that will obviously leave them hurting pretty bad.<br /> <br /> That would make it just basically a better version of Vigor, but this doesn't seem to occupy much of a design space other than that.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you may want to look at the new Invictus devotions that David Hill unveiled, as one of them seems to take this same idea but in a direction that feels more fleshed out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I know I sound critical, but I absolutely laud the &quot;yes, and...&quot; Approach to storytelling, I'm just trying to offer my thoughts so that you can bring down thing to your table that could be more fun. Devotions are ideally interesting/creative, and I think the key for this one is to make it have some kind of additional effect against mortal's to reflect a greater capacity for harm which then translates into the increased lethality against Kindred. <br /> <br /> I dig the idea of a way that would inflict Tilts as being one of the ways to dial up the lethality.<br /> <br /> Another way to do it could be a devotion that enhances the active effect against Mortal's? So it automatically can inflict a tilt like Arm Wrack to reflect the bodily harm in them, and to Kindred it allows you to do lethal where you'd otherwise do bashing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: one finally note: in a fight between the guy with Protean 4 class and Vigor 4, the guy with Protean is gonna have a pretty hard time winning. The guy with Vigor 4 will always have a larger dice pool and will hit for much more raw damage, so that's something to keep in mind. Without a large amount of Resilience, the Protean guy is gonna have a very bad day most of the time against the vigor guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-16-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:58:47-08:00","id":811450,"title":"","content":"The feedback is appreciated, as is the acknowledgement of the &quot;Yes, and . . .&quot; school of thought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This here is some useful food for thought on how to modify the Devotion idea. I do agree it's simplistic (and even I think it is redundant w/r/t Vigor itself; the above draft is a starting point), so having something more (like the Vigor - 2 modifier) and/or the Tilt idea is a good approach. I'll also have to look at the Invictus Devotions since I haven't seen them yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}